<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4297] .NET: Upgrading NuGet to new version does not clean up jar files in bin folder</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4297</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Apache.Ignite.Core NuGet package updates post-build step with a script to copy jar files to the bin directory.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, this script does not remove old versions of jar files. This causes a problem when upgrading to a new version of NuGet package: user gets an error like&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;Failed to initialize JVM. ---&amp;gt; Apache.Ignite.Core.Common.IgniteException: Java &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;class &lt;/span&gt;method is not found (did you set IGNITE_HOME environment variable?): binaryProcessor ---&amp;gt; Apache.Ignite.Core.Common.JavaException: java.lang.NoSuchMethodError: binaryProcessor
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
